{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7JdSo2vtPMBNZcB4ND","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `auth.0011_update_proxy_permissions` so it no longer hits the duplicate-key error on proxy models that already have permissions.\n\nThe migration now looks up which permission codenames already exist for the proxy model's content type. It skips those when moving permissions over from the concrete model's content type. This avoids the unique-constraint violation on `(content_type_id, codename)`.\n\nThe existing `auth_tests.test_migrations` tests pass. I didn't add a test for the duplicate case, and I haven't run it against a database that actually has duplicate permissions.\n\nThe change is in `django/contrib/auth/migrations/0011_update_proxy_permissions.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1335,"cache_read_input_tokens":19337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1335},"output_tokens":219,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59747967-0a89-43c6-b8dc-0528bd9a56c9","uuid":"2b50eaa5-0ffe-45bf-9167-82236b9b31b0","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:57:44.127Z","request_id":"req_011ChK7JdJc6qCQ7MGpuNQZi"}
